# Conformance probe pack for range sentinels in `absent` (spec 0.56) on `xml`:
# a leading `=` before `>=`. Public. No kinds. Added because the 0.56 probe
# packs have no wire that strips `=`: `absent =>=5` on a string key is the
# exact text `>=5` (Version 0.56, "absent by range", the sentence on `=>=5`),
# so the text `>=5` is absent, the number text 7 is present, and an absent
# key writes `>=5`.
format  conformance-absent-range-056-1
version 0.56.0
distribution public
source  "goat-transformers spec/engine-spec.md (synthetic probe format, no external standard)"
uses    probe
wire    xml
root    msg
field   uid          @uid    string
field   probe.label  @label  string  absent =>=5
